0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nreproducible on v4.7.dev.custom_build [ebc126193]\nnot reproducible in v4.6.1.stable.arch_linux [14d19694e]\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev (ebc126193) - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Mon, 09 Feb 2026 17:16:33 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon 780M Graphics (radeonsi, phoenix, LLVM 21.1.6, DRM 3.64, 6.18.9-arch1-2) - AMD Ryzen 7 8745HS w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 threads) - 28.18 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n\n<img width=\"1459\" height=\"1010\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8b4ab59e-4a40-47cf-afee-e3760b8e190b\" />\n\nThe variable `node reference` is not null, but doesn't show in the inspector when viewing the remote tree. The `@exported` variable shows fine though\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSet a variable value with `get_child` during runtime, and try to view it in the remote inspector. The variable value doesn't show, even if it can be printed just fine.\n\n```swift\nvar node_reference\nfunc _ready():\n    node_reference = get_child(0)\n    print(node_reference)\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n(project started from a project linked in this similar issue https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/77580)\n\n[treeexpander_2026-02-26_13-50-06.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25585158/treeexpander_2026-02-26_13-50-06.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repi